  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\"><a class=\"vis-app\" href=\"cl_ara_core_Result_d51722.html\">Result</a>&lt; void, <a href=\"#class-decl\">E</a> &gt; GetResult () noexcept(<a class=\"cppref\" href=\"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/is_move_constructible\" title=\"cppreference.com (C++17)\">std::is_nothrow_move_ constructible</a>&lt; <a href=\"#class-decl\">E</a> &gt;::value);</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Get the result. Similar to Future::get(), this call blocks until the value or an error is available. However, this call will never throw an exception. Part of the behavior taken from Future::get() is that after a call to this function the Future is not valid anymore (valid() == false).</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
